  "instance_name": "dishwasher_metaphor",
  "label": "Dishwasher Metaphor",
  "description": "The use of the dishwasher as a metaphor for a woman’s body being 'ready' for another load — a play on the literal function of a dishwasher (which needs to be loaded with dishes) and the figurative meaning of being 'ready' for something. This metaphor relies on the viewer understanding the double entendre and the cultural association of women’s bodies with domestic labor and availability.",
